cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use PurpleForge in academic work, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
title: >
  PurpleForge: A reproducible, quantitatively-evaluated purple-team
  assessment framework with cross-source normalised findings
authors:
  - name: "PurpleForge Contributors"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-04-07"
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/purpleforge/purpleforge"
keywords:
  - purple team
  - security assessment
  - reproducibility
  - ATT&CK
  - defensive evaluation
  - ethical hacking
  - SBOM
  - audit log
abstract: >
  PurpleForge is a CLI-first, ethically-constrained purple-team assessment
  platform designed for authorized defensive evaluation and academic research.
  It enforces ownership verification before any web-target interaction,
  produces hash-chained JSONL audit logs, correlates telemetry against
  ATT&CK techniques, and generates quantitative coverage metrics across
  assessment campaigns. All nine implementation phases are covered by 370+
  automated tests with a CI pipeline on Python 3.11 and 3.12.
